  "Born Brian O'Nolan at Strabane, County Tyrone, on 5 April 1911; he entered the Irish civil service and published At Swim-Two-Birds in 1939, the experimental novel of the author and his characters. As 'Myles na gCopaleen' he wrote the Cruiskeen Lawn column in The Irish Times from 1940 and the Abbey play Faustus Kelly (1943); The Third Policeman, written in the war years, was published only after his death. He died in Dublin on 1 April 1966.",
  "Flann O'Brien is the great experimental comic novelist of Ireland: At Swim-Two-Birds made the novel of the author and his characters the form of the Irish modernism, the Cruiskeen Lawn column is the finest comic journalism in Irish English, and The Third Policeman, written in the war years, is the comic metaphysic of the police and the bicycle.",
